<BaseLayout title="About AI Workflow Toolkit" description="Why AI Workflow Toolkit focuses on documented, testable and safer business automation blueprints.">
<div class="wrap"><div class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">About the project</span><h1>Make automation <span class="gradient">clear before it goes live.</span></h1><p>AI Workflow Toolkit is an independent early-stage project exploring a practical gap: teams need more than a list of connected apps. They need a clear trigger, ownership, failure handling, approval rules and tests.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/builder/">Try the builder ↗</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://github.com/piyushnath227/ai-workflow-toolkit" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the code</a></div></div><article class="article"><h2>Our approach</h2><ul><li>Document the workflow and expected outcome.</li><li>Prevent duplicate events and define safe retry behavior.</li><li>Keep human approval for sensitive or irreversible actions.</li><li>Verify the outcome instead of trusting a success message.</li><li>Be explicit when a feature is a plan, scaffold or live integration.</li></ul><h2>Current stage</h2><p>This is an early product. The rule-based browser builder and starter blueprints are available; optional AI generation and D1-backed endpoints require Cloudflare configuration. Template exports are scaffolds until imported and tested in the target n8n environment.</p></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
